     -oo _f_i_l_e
          Write the output into _f_i_l_e instead of the default,
          ll.oouutt.

     -rr   Retain relocation information in the output and do not
          complain about undefined symbols; produces a .oo file as
          if its pieces had been compiled together.

     -RR _b_a_s_e
          Set the relocation base of the output to _b_a_s_e (a symbol
          name or a number) instead of the machine's usual
          default.

     -ss   Discard the symbol table from the output.

     -uu _s_y_m
          Add _s_y_m to the symbol table as an undefined global
          reference, to force a library search that pulls in
          whichever module defines it -- for example, -uu _ddttooaa_,
          to force the real floating-point formatter ahead of its
          stub in lliibbcc.aa.

     -ww   Watch: print progress messages (module and undefined-
          symbol counts, final image size) as linking proceeds.
          This option is accepted by the program but is not
          listed in the Options table above.

     -XX   Discard C-internal local symbols.

     -xx   Discard all local symbols.

